		{"type":"text","text":"1. absolute temperature T\n2. the ratio between the gravitational compression time t_comp and the radiative cooling time t_cool \n3. entropy criterion","id":"28fbfdfc81f78451","x":-280,"y":2423,"width":405,"height":105},
		{"type":"text","text":"1. lyman alpha\n2. GSMF","id":"8a72566fa83d492d","x":-280,"y":2795,"width":320,"height":55},
		{"type":"text","text":"observation","id":"e61b21a2b5c9e524","x":-600,"y":2795,"width":140,"height":50},
		{"type":"text","text":"1. the gas as it falls through the halo is qualitatively different below and above a critical mass scale of **Mshock $10^{12} M_\\odot$** (Birnboim & Dekel 2003; Kereˇs et al. 2005).\n2. In less massive haloes, the disc is built by cold flows (∼10^4−5 K), infalling gas heated by shock in massive haloes near the virial temperature (∼10^6 K)\n3. Near and above Mshock at z>2 (and preferentially in isolated galaxies), streams of dense cold gas penetrate through the dilute shockheated medium","id":"1f02fafe72b4d094","x":-280,"y":2550,"width":460,"height":210}
	],
